        "answer": "PPR scoring stands for \"points per reception.\" In this fantasy football format, every catch a player makes is worth one additional point on top of the standard scoring values. This system increases the value of players who catch a lot of passes, such as high-volume receivers and pass-catching running backs.\n\nFor example, a slot receiver with ten catches for sixty yards would score six points in standard scoring, but sixteen points in PPR\u2014nearly three times as much for the same game.\n\nThis information is from the fantasy scoring formats reference, updated as of September 27, 2026."
